WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.418
Laura Riley: Oh, this is my favorite.

00:00:02.418 --> 00:00:05.180
"Pregnant women need
to eat twice as much."

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.293
Absolute myth.

00:00:06.293 --> 00:00:07.592
Don't do it.

00:00:07.592 --> 00:00:11.610
You really actually only need
about 200 extra calories a day

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.680
over a normal American diet.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.740
And that's assuming that
you're starting pregnancy

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.790
at a normal weight.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.710
"Sex during pregnancy hurts the baby."

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:20.543
Well...

00:00:20.543 --> 00:00:22.770
Dena Goffman: "Cocoa butter
prevents stretch marks."

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:23.820
This is a myth.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.780
I'm Laura Riley.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.180
I'm a high-risk OB

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.270
at New York-Presbyterian
Hospital/Weill Cornell.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.430
I'm Dena Goffman.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.497
I'm a high-risk OB at New
York Presbyterian/Columbia.

00:00:33.497 --> 00:00:34.538
This is so exciting,

00:00:34.538 --> 00:00:35.715
wondering what's gonna come next.

00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:37.020
Riley: I know, I know.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.550
Goffman: Oh, my favorite.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.760
"It's OK to drink a glass of
wine when you're pregnant."

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.390
We know that the recommendation
in pregnancy is that

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.660
you really should not consume any alcohol.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:50.660
Unfortunately, there is
no safe amount of alcohol

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.600
nor a safe time in pregnancy
when we can be sure

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.030
that alcohol won't affect
a developing fetus.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.100
Riley: Also, I think it's important to add

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.630
that we don't think it's safe to drink

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:03.910
while you're breastfeeding, either,

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:07.480
because the alcohol does
get into breast milk.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.920
And as Dr. Goffman said,

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.350
we don't know what the safe
amount is, and that safe amount

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:16.600
may actually change for different women.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.890
Goffman: "Your belly
reveals the baby's gender."

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:21.320
We certainly hear patients
coming in to see us

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.750
and having heard or
having family members say

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.660
that they can tell whether
you're having a boy

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:29.400
or a girl based on how
the woman's belly looks.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.890
And we know that there
is absolutely no evidence

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.600
that the shape of your belly can tell us

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.190
this type of information.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.510
Riley: The other myth that
goes along with gender

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.003
I think is the heart rate is high or low.

00:01:41.003 --> 00:01:43.190
My patients always say that,
you know, they come in,

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:46.640
oh, it's 160, it must be girl.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:50.750
Like, no. If it's 160, it
means the kid's moving a lot,

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.750
and if it's sleeping it's going to be 120.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.250
So it doesn't tell you
whether it's a girl or boy.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:58.780
Goffman: "Cocoa butter
prevents stretch marks."

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.530
This is a myth.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.986
While cocoa butter is something

00:02:02.986 --> 00:02:04.986
that many patients like to use,

00:02:04.986 --> 00:02:07.594
we don't have any
evidence that cocoa butter

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.440
or anything else that we can recommend

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.120
will prevent stretch marks.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.810
Riley: It's probably
genetic, and, essentially,

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:17.080
if you gain too much weight in one spot,

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.500
i.e. your pregnancy gets really big,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.430
you're more likely to get
stretch marks, unfortunately.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.240
But it's not worth spending a ton of money

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:28.260
on expensive creams,
because it's not gonna work.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.210
That was cheery.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:33.700
"You can give a cold to
your developing baby."

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.630
This is a complete myth.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:38.820
Your baby is not gonna get the cold.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.740
Although your baby can get sick

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.890
if you get something like the flu,

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:46.240
which is why we tell
you to get a flu shot,

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.640
to prevent your baby
from getting really sick.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.410
There are some illnesses you can transfer

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:53.070
to your baby, but probably not a cold.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.100
I think people get the
cold and the flu confused,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.230
which is unfortunate because the flu

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.310
can make you really sick in pregnancy.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:01.980
Goffman: "What you eat during pregnancy

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.190
can influence the baby's palate."

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.900
Riley: I don't think there
is a shred of evidence

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.470
to support that.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:11.560
I think that what you eat
during pregnancy is important

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.118
because it does sort of, you know,

00:03:14.118 --> 00:03:16.884
set your baby off to a good start

00:03:16.884 --> 00:03:20.803
in terms of its overall
nutrition and good health.

00:03:20.803 --> 00:03:23.510
But it's probably not gonna
change the baby's palate.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.270
Goffman: We always talk about
nutrition and food choices

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.320
and healthy weight gain,

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:29.500
which really can have long-term impact

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.590
on your baby's development,
but not specifically the palate

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.290
or what they have a taste for.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.610
Riley: "Pregnant women
shouldn't drink coffee."

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.580
That's a myth.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.970
You can drink coffee.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:43.620
This is one where moderation
is the most important thing.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.770
In the first trimester, having
excessive amounts of coffee

00:03:47.770 --> 00:03:50.810
have been associated with a
higher risk of miscarriage.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:53.260
Once that first trimester is over,

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.660
should you go crazy with the coffee?

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.010
Probably not.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.130
But it's not gonna harm anything.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.540
Goffman: "Pregnant women
shouldn't eat hot dogs."

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.760
So, this is a myth.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.810
I think the concern
with hot dogs are a few.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.030
You want to make sure
that they are well cooked

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.890
to avoid infection risk.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.050
And there used to be a
fair amount of conversation

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.130
about the amount of nitrites in hot dogs,

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.990
but I think the evidence suggests
that unless you're eating

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.870
really excessive amounts of hot dogs,

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.606
that it's probably OK to enjoy one.

00:04:19.606 --> 00:04:21.611
I think there are probably things

00:04:21.611 --> 00:04:23.803
better than hot dogs
to eat, nutritionally,

00:04:23.803 --> 00:04:26.462
but I think if people
enjoy one once in a while,

00:04:26.462 --> 00:04:28.270
I don't have a problem with it.

00:04:28.270 --> 00:04:30.328
Riley: You're way nicer than I am.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.170
I'm not sure why anybody's
eating hot dogs, frankly,

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.410
but, you know, you can
have one in pregnancy,

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.633
but I think it's really important

00:04:38.633 --> 00:04:40.071
to make sure that it's cooked,

00:04:40.071 --> 00:04:44.120
because the concern about
listeria is a real concern.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.210
So, that includes the hot dogs,

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:49.560
the unpasteurized cheeses, the deli meats.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.930
All of those things are
things that we worry about.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.400
So I think, you know.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.872
Yeah, it's a myth that
you can't eat hot dogs,

00:04:55.872 --> 00:04:59.500
but you should be certain
that it's cooked well.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:02.270
"Pregnant women shouldn't
eat smoked salmon."

00:05:02.270 --> 00:05:03.300
That's a myth.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.970
You can eat smoked salmon if you like it.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:07.680
I'm not a lover of salmon, so.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:08.730
Goffman: I love it.

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:10.160
You can eat smoked salmon.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.330
This gets into concerns
around fish consumption

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.400
in pregnancy, which is a huge topic.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.000
And we talk to our patients about the risk

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.890
of various types of fish.

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:22.780
So, we want to avoid fish
with high mercury content.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.340
So typically that would be
avoiding excessive tuna,

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.210
choosing chunk-light, canned tuna,

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:32.780
and also limiting the number
of cans of tuna in a week.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:37.070
There is also some concern
about some of these oily fish,

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:39.920
I guess, about the potential for toxins.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.150
And so I would say salmon
in general may fall

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.380
into that category, but
smoked salmon I think is safe

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:46.930
for pregnant women to eat.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.746
Riley: The whole fish story is a little

00:05:49.746 --> 00:05:51.146
blown out of proportion.

00:05:51.146 --> 00:05:53.440
And I think people get really crazy

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.110
about this whole mercury thing.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.990
I would say it's important
to also recognize, though,

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.570
that fish has great
nutritional value to it

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:05.790
that pregnant women and
babies need and want.

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:09.930
So it is unfortunate that
somehow the fish story

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.860
has resulted in people thinking,
"I can't have any fish."

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.760
It's really the large steak fishes

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.530
where you're worried about the mercury.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:20.240
But then, don't forget
that something like salmon

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:23.770
is gonna give you the
DHEAS, which you want.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.810
Goffman: "Pregnant women
shouldn't pet cats."

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:26.920
This is a myth.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.170
This would be terrible
if all pregnant women

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:32.990
in the world couldn't pet
their pets, their cats.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.190
There is a concern with
pregnant women caring

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.980
for cats in terms of the litter box,

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.470
and really the risk is toxoplasmosis.

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:42.180
And the risk of exposure
isn't with interacting

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.030
with your cat, but with
changing a dirty litter box.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.860
Riley: It is actually
fairly rare in the US

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:51.400
for women to come into
contact with toxoplasmosis.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:54.520
The more important thing
about sort of the cat stories,

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:57.229
everyone worries about the
cat and the kitty litter;

00:06:57.229 --> 00:07:00.037
the most common exposure

00:07:00.037 --> 00:07:02.770
that women get to toxoplasmosis

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.095
is actually not the cat or the liter even.

00:07:06.095 --> 00:07:09.395
It's not washing your garden vegetables,

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:11.653
because it's the cat that has the toxin

00:07:11.653 --> 00:07:13.911
that poops in your garden

00:07:13.911 --> 00:07:16.940
and then you pick that up and eat it

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:18.390
because you don't wash it or whatever.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:21.390
So, gardening without gloves are things

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.750
that we tell pregnant women to avoid

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.560
because of that particular infection.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.820
The cat's got a bad rap, unfortunately.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.260
"Pregnant women shouldn't fly."

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:32.110
Total myth, get on the
plane, have a good time.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:34.640
That said, there are a few things

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.590
to think about when flying.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:40.730
I think one of the major
issues is that pregnant women

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.098
are at increased risk
for getting a blood clot

00:07:43.098 --> 00:07:45.140
either in their leg or their lung.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:48.560
When you fly, the air is dry.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.050
You're also more likely just to be sitting

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:53.340
for a prolonged period of time.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:56.030
And that just further increases your risk

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.000
for getting a blood clot.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.290
So I always tell pregnant
women, be happy, go ahead.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.540
Go on those trips.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:04.470
But you should hydrate before you go.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:05.869
You should wear support hose

00:08:05.869 --> 00:08:08.611
or at least, like, you
know, running tights

00:08:08.611 --> 00:08:10.758
or something that gives
you a little bit of

00:08:10.758 --> 00:08:12.260
support in your legs.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:15.880
You should get up and walk
around every hour or so.

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:18.360
People worry about the air pressure,

00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:20.700
which makes no sense because
it's a pressurized cabin.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.590
That doesn't do anything,

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.920
you're not gonna break your water.

00:08:22.920 --> 00:08:26.730
And they also worry about going
through the screener, right?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.150
Everybody's worried about the radiation

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:29.983
going through the screener,

00:08:29.983 --> 00:08:33.530
but in fact the radiation
exposure is actually higher

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:36.590
when you're in the sky
in the plane than it is

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.412
when you're walking quickly

00:08:38.412 --> 00:08:40.310
through the security.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:43.470
Goffman: "Exercise during
pregnancy can strangle the baby."

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:45.770
This is a myth.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.710
Exercise is actually strongly
recommended during pregnancy.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.440
All of our professional organizations,

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:53.590
all of us as providers talk to patients

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:55.910
about maintaining physical activity,

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:58.090
maintaining exercise
throughout the pregnancy,

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:01.420
really unless there's a medical situation

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:03.850
that comes up that changes
those recommendations.

00:09:03.850 --> 00:09:06.030
So, exercise is not dangerous.

00:09:06.030 --> 00:09:07.510
And in fact, the opposite.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:08.950
It's really important.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:11.610
Riley: I think also this
whole strangling thing comes

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.180
from this crazy nonsense
that if you get yourself

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.250
into certain yoga positions,

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:18.770
your baby can strangle itself.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:20.250
You don't have any control

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.200
over the position your baby gets into.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.910
The baby is floating in a pool of water.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.650
And it doesn't matter whether
you're doing a headstand

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.540
or you're just, like, chilling.

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.440
"Sex during pregnancy hurts the baby."

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:34.320
Well, that's a big myth.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.780
And it also helps to understand

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.420
sort of the anatomy a little bit.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:41.220
I think this is where patients
get a little bit confused.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:44.940
The baby is floating
inside a pool of water,

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.820
a big balloon bag.

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:50.910
And that balloon bag is
surrounded by thick muscle,

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:55.500
which is the uterus,
surrounds the entire bag

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.210
and has, actually, a thicker
portion at the bottom.

00:09:58.210 --> 00:09:59.960
So there's just no way

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:03.250
that sex is gonna get even near the baby.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.700
Goffman: Dyeing your hair
is harmful for the baby.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:06.910
This is another big myth.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.250
And we get phone calls about it.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.460
Lots of questions.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:10.680
There is no evidence, and again,

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:11.960
we keep coming back to evidence

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.140
because that's what we
look to as your physicians.

00:10:15.140 --> 00:10:16.720
And there really is no evidence out there

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.570
that the things that we use
for hair-dyeing reach the baby

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.250
or have the potential to cause harm.

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:23.590
Riley: The other thing about the hair dye,

00:10:23.590 --> 00:10:26.930
frankly, I tell people, if it's
gonna make you feel better,

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:30.677
that's really important
because, for a lot of us,

00:10:30.677 --> 00:10:33.060
how we look and how we present ourselves

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:35.960
really has a lot to do with
our psychological state.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:37.220
And you want that to be

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.410
as healthy as possible during pregnancy.

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.780
"There are simple tricks to
overcome morning sickness."

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:44.430
I think that that's a myth in the sense

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:47.200
that none of those things
were probably simple.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.830
But I think there are ways

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:53.830
to sort of decrease the
painfulness of morning sickness.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.690
The first thing is that
the morning sickness

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:56.710
can last all day,

00:10:56.710 --> 00:11:00.650
so the whole "morning" thing
is a myth in and of itself.

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:03.390
But that said, some of the things

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:06.100
that you can do to help it:

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:09.880
Try and start the day with
something really simple,

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.480
like soda crackers, the
minute you get out of bed.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.300
Saltines, something really bland.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:16.930
Stay away from the smells,

00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:18.580
the smells are going to make you sicker.

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.280
I think the biggest
thing that I've learned

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:21.505
over the course of my career,

00:11:21.505 --> 00:11:24.421
and had personal
involvement with this one,

00:11:24.421 --> 00:11:26.320
is we tell people to stay hydrated

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:28.620
and so they go after the water bottle.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.200
And stay away from the water.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.640
The water makes you sick,
I don't understand it,

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:34.980
but it makes you sick.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:38.480
So, what I tell patients is put
everything over crushed ice.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.020
That way you'll get the water

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:42.830
but you're not actually
drinking it and gulping air

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:44.630
as you're drinking out of a water bottle.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.500
The things that I would put over ice,

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:49.410
I would say lemonade, and ginger ale,

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:52.300
letting some of the fizz
out, will help as well.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:55.950
Lemon Popsicles, lemon
slush, lemon Italian ice.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:57.450
The reason I say lemon is because lemon

00:11:57.450 --> 00:11:59.160
helps cut the nausea as well.

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.610
I think the other critical thing

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:02.500
for morning sickness is

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.000
it's important to go out every day.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.391
I think sometimes what happens is

00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:06.733
you feel a little bit nauseous,

00:12:06.733 --> 00:12:10.020
then you feel worse, then
you start to feel depressed,

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:12.910
and then you can't get yourself
moving because you're tired.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:14.360
And that's the worst thing you can do

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:16.130
is to sort of give in to it.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.410
I think it's important to
get outside, walk around,

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:20.450
even if it's just down the block and back.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:22.691
Goffman: "C-sections are always necessary

00:12:22.691 --> 00:12:24.091
for breech births."

00:12:24.091 --> 00:12:27.450
So, this is a myth,
although I think most of us

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:30.961
think C-sections are the most common

00:12:30.961 --> 00:12:34.790
and the safest way to deliver a singleton.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:39.230
So, a single baby in
labor, especially at term.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.910
So there are certainly situations

00:12:40.910 --> 00:12:43.100
that we need to be able
to individualize for.

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:45.210
Often we'll talk to patients with twins.

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.880
If the second twin is breech,

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:49.315
that may be a great option for them.

00:12:49.315 --> 00:12:51.050
And I think there are rare situations

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.934
where a woman comes in in labor

00:12:52.934 --> 00:12:56.191
where we may recommend and or support

00:12:56.191 --> 00:12:58.680
a vaginal breech delivery for a singleton.

00:12:58.680 --> 00:12:59.822
Riley: I think in order to support

00:12:59.822 --> 00:13:01.055
a vaginal breech delivery,

00:13:01.055 --> 00:13:04.620
you need to have a provider
who has experience doing that.

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:07.750
And, you know, the
reality is that in the US,

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:11.470
the number of providers that
are able to do those safely

00:13:11.470 --> 00:13:15.910
is definitely diminishing, almost to none.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.260
I think the other option though,

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:20.400
which I think we should
put out there on the table,

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:22.649
is a version which is

00:13:22.649 --> 00:13:26.133
if you know the baby is
breech and you're at term,

00:13:26.133 --> 00:13:28.680
is coming in for a procedure where we,

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:32.450
under ultrasound guidance,
turn the baby to head-down.

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.483
"If you sit all day,
you'll have a breech baby."

00:13:37.392 --> 00:13:38.540
Total myth.

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:41.350
If you sit all day, you'll
gain a lot of weight

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:42.700
and you'll have back pain,

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.550
but your baby will do whatever
your baby is gonna do.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:48.560
Most babies are not breech at full term.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:52.001
So, only about, is it like 3% of babies

00:13:52.001 --> 00:13:54.643
are gonna be breech at full term.

00:13:54.643 --> 00:13:57.140
Those babies are gonna turn multiple times

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:00.570
until they get to around 36 or 37 weeks.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.380
And so it has nothing to do

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.090
with whether you're running a marathon

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:05.960
or you're sitting on your bottom.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:08.720
Goffman: "Pregnant women should
sleep on their left side."

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:11.720
I think pregnant women should
sleep how they're comfortable,

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:15.180
although we know that women,
as they get more pregnant

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:17.730
into the second and certainly
in the third trimester,

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:20.320
may not be able to sleep
flat on their back.

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:23.370
And that's because as the
pregnancy grows, the fetus grows,

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.610
the uterus grows, the
weight that the uterus

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.420
will put on your blood vessels

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:29.520
and some other structures may make that

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:32.780
really uncomfortable and
not ideal for the baby.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:34.630
So women can sleep on their left side,

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:35.950
they can sleep on their right side,

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:38.410
they can sleep on their
back, tilted a little bit.

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:40.640
But we usually aren't so strict

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:42.013
as to say left side only.

00:14:42.013 --> 00:14:44.610
Riley: I think people
worry that, oh, my gosh,

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:48.320
I woke up and I'm flat on
my back, did I kill my baby?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.410
You didn't kill your baby.

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:53.450
If you sleep flat on your
back, as Dr. Goffman said,

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.760
the structure we're most worried

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.440
about is the inferior vena cava,

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.840
so it's this big blood
vessel bringing blood back up

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.140
to your heart and your head.

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:04.275
And most people are gonna
get really nauseous, right?

00:15:04.275 --> 00:15:05.840
And light-headed and feel weird.

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.955
And so you'll naturally turn,

00:15:07.955 --> 00:15:10.290
so you don't have to wake
yourself up to do it.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:14.067
"Your hair and skin look
better when you're pregnant."

00:15:14.067 --> 00:15:15.260
Ha, I wish.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:18.120
Your hair might look better, I guess?

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:21.002
Your skin probably won't
necessarily look better.

00:15:21.002 --> 00:15:22.583
Some women say they glow.

00:15:22.583 --> 00:15:24.640
I think that they're...[laughs]
they're dreaming.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.550
Unfortunately, the high
progesterone levels

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.760
that you get when you're pregnant

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:33.920
to support the pregnancy actually
can really bring out acne

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:36.610
that you haven't seen since
you were 13 years old,

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:38.350
and all the expensive creams

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.160
in the world are not gonna fix that.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.280
So I wouldn't suggest that
you spend your money on it.

00:15:42.280 --> 00:15:44.320
Goffman: "Pregnant women get flexible."

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:47.150
You know, we recognize there
are lots of changes going on

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:49.260
in women's bodies when they're pregnant,

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.160
but I wouldn't say that getting
flexible is one of them.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.390
There are certain things that happen

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:56.100
in terms of your posture,
how you stand, and definitely

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.530
some relaxation of
different parts of your body

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:03.530
to prepare your pelvis to be
able to have a vaginal birth.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.140
But I don't think that sort
of traditional flexibility

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:08.010
is what we typically see.

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.470
"Eating spicy foods will induce labor."

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.480
Riley: Ha!

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.030
Goffman: So, if this were
true, that would be wonderful

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:17.720
because we could help women
induce labor when we wanted to.

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.880
Unfortunately, we haven't
been able to come up

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:24.290
with any particular food or
physical activity or drink

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:27.060
or supplement that
actually can induce labor.

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:29.990
We have medications to
use to induce labor,

00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:31.780
but as far as we've been able to tell,

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:34.030
there is no evidence
that any of those things

00:16:34.030 --> 00:16:37.890
that women may want to try
actually will be effective.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.310
Riley: I think people are
just looking for something

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:42.390
to get out of Dodge at 40 weeks,

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:44.216
which I can totally relate to.

00:16:44.216 --> 00:16:45.049
Goffman: Yeah.

00:16:45.049 --> 00:16:46.380
[laughing]

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:47.670
It's not going to hurt.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:48.810
Riley: It's probably not going to hurt.

00:16:48.810 --> 00:16:51.040
The spicy food probably won't hurt.

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:53.300
You can do whatever you want,
but your baby's in charge.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.690
Just remember that.

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.290
Goffman: "Yoga can induce labor."

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:58.140
We think there are a lot of benefits

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:01.930
to potentially doing yoga and
participating in pregnancy,

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:03.960
but inducing labor isn't one of them.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.820
Certainly more women are using yoga,

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:09.130
which may help with relaxation,
may help with stress relief,

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.790
may help with stretching.

00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:12.360
And so I think there are a lot of reasons

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:15.410
why yoga may be a great
thing to participate in,

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:18.832
but there's no evidence
that it induces labor.

00:17:18.832 --> 00:17:20.350
Riley: If only.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.490
"Yoga makes labor smoother."

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.622
I think, overall,

00:17:24.622 --> 00:17:29.022
exercise probably gives you a better labor

00:17:29.022 --> 00:17:32.570
in the sense that it is
usually more efficient.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:37.570
But yoga itself, not
necessarily making it smoother.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.940
Goffman: There are some things
about yoga that are similar

00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:43.500
to other labor preparation

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.872
or childbirth preparation things, right?

00:17:45.872 --> 00:17:49.260
Breathing, mindfulness,
I think are similar

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:51.980
to some childbirth preparation things.

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.430
So I think, in that sense, some
of those things may help you

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:56.560
to be more centered, be able to focus,

00:17:56.560 --> 00:17:58.640
be able to use some of
those strategies to help,

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.640
but certainly not make
labor itself smoother.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:06.270
"Natural births are better."

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.340
So, this is a myth.

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:11.490
There are certainly women who

00:18:11.490 --> 00:18:13.356
spend time thinking

00:18:13.356 --> 00:18:16.490
about what they'd like their
birth experience to be like.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.660
And I think for some women, natural birth,

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.700
and the way we think about
that is usually birth

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.310
without pain medication,
and for some women,

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:26.430
this may be a wonderful
experience, but we all know

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.890
that we need to individualize
the care for our patients.

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:31.890
And for many women, a natural
birth may not be better.

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:34.485
There may be real medical benefits,

00:18:34.485 --> 00:18:38.310
depending on the situation
and underlying condition,

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:42.220
to having pain medication,
to having an epidural.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:45.660
Riley: I'm a huge fan of natural
childbirth, I have to say,

00:18:45.660 --> 00:18:47.570
but I do think that it
takes some preparation,

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:49.560
and I think it takes mental preparation,

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.870
and I think that it's not better or worse.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:57.590
I also think there's
another myth associated

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:02.050
with natural childbirth, which
is that if you're induced

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:05.880
you have to have anesthesia
because the pain is worse.

00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:10.640
The pain is bad whether we
give you the contractions

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:12.380
or your kid gives you the contractions

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.450
or it happens naturally, whatever.

00:19:14.450 --> 00:19:15.360
It's painful.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:19.600
And some people can cope better

00:19:19.600 --> 00:19:21.950
because they've practiced mindfulness

00:19:21.950 --> 00:19:25.060
or hypnobirthing or whatever.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.990
And then sometimes people
can just cope better

00:19:26.990 --> 00:19:27.940
because it's faster.

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:29.351
But again, I think it's all about

00:19:29.351 --> 00:19:32.550
everybody can make
their own birth choices.

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:33.510
I love this one.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:37.700
"There are ways to predict
your exact due date."

00:19:37.700 --> 00:19:38.880
When we give you your due date,

00:19:38.880 --> 00:19:40.740
it's plus or minus two weeks.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:42.598
And the reason is because
your kid's in charge

00:19:42.598 --> 00:19:43.960
of when you go into labor.

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:45.070
We are not.

00:19:45.070 --> 00:19:48.570
Though, I have to say, are
much more precise in knowing

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:51.150
what your dates are than we used to be

00:19:51.150 --> 00:19:54.340
because we use ultrasound,
early, early ultrasounds,

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:55.900
so much more frequently.

00:19:55.900 --> 00:19:58.240
Obviously, there are those
people who have done IVF,

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.170
and they know even more.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.870
But again, even if you
know when it all started,

00:20:02.870 --> 00:20:05.370
you do not know when it will all end.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.910
Because the person who
knows that is your baby

00:20:07.910 --> 00:20:12.400
and we can't at the moment
talk to that person.

00:20:39.056 --> 00:20:39.889
Goffman: This is so exciting,

00:20:39.889 --> 00:20:41.020
wondering what's gonna come next.

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:42.437
Riley: I know, I know.

